IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p5-administration`
IMPORT `sca-p6-supplemental`

-- Tests for Part 5 (ss 57 to 68) and Part 6 (s 70).  Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion, never from the code's output.

§ `Section 57`

#ASSERT `s 57(1) the Registry of the State Courts is to be open on the day` `Ordinary day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(1) the Registry of the State Courts is to be open on the day` Saturday EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 57(1) the Registry of the State Courts is to be open on the day` Sunday EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 57(1) the Registry of the State Courts is to be open on the day` `Public holiday` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 57(1) the Registry of the State Courts is to be open on the day` `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 57(2): a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday; directed; urgent in the registrar's opinion.
#ASSERT `s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` Saturday TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` Sunday FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` `Public holiday` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` Saturday FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` `Ordinary day` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 57(2) the registrar may lawfully sit or carry out the business of the Registry on the day` `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 57(3) the time is within the office hours of the Registry` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(3) the time is within the office hours of the Registry` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 58 to 61`

#ASSERT `s 58 both civil and criminal proceedings may be tried at the sitting of the court` `District Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 both civil and criminal proceedings may be tried at the sitting of the court` `Magistrate's Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 both civil and criminal proceedings may be tried at the sitting of the court` `Coroner's Court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 59 the distribution of business in the State Courts has been made in accordance with the directions as the section requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59 the distribution of business in the State Courts has been made in accordance with the directions as the section requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 61: 15 days is the ceiling.
#ASSERT `s 61 the Chief Justice may authorise the vacations` TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61 the Chief Justice may authorise the vacations` TRUE 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61 the Chief Justice may authorise the vacations` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61 the Chief Justice may authorise the vacations` FALSE 10 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 62`

#ASSERT `s 62(1) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may frame, publish, alter and amend the list of touts` `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(1) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may frame, publish, alter and amend the list of touts` `District Judge` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(1)(a) the person may be named in the list of touts` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(1)(a) the person may be named in the list of touts` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 62(2): the person is named in the list; the person is a party or a witness.
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may exclude the person from the precincts of the State Courts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may exclude the person from the precincts of the State Courts` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may exclude the person from the precincts of the State Courts` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is allowed to remain in the precincts of the State Courts for such time as is necessary` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is allowed to remain in the precincts of the State Courts for such time as is necessary` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(2) the person is allowed to remain in the precincts of the State Courts for such time as is necessary` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(3) the person's name may be included in the list of touts` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 62(3) the person's name may be included in the list of touts` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(4) an appeal lies to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division of the High Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(4) an appeal lies to a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division of the High Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(5) the decision of the Judge is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(5) the decision of the Judge is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(6) a copy of the list is kept hung up and the list has been published in the Gazette as the section requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(6) a copy of the list is kept hung up and the list has been published in the Gazette as the section requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(6) a copy of the list is kept hung up and the list has been published in the Gazette as the section requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under this section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under this section` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under section 73 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 or section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(7) the person is deemed to be included in the list under section 73 of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 or section 39 of the Family Justice Act 2014` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 63`

#ASSERT `s 63(1) a State Court may order the document to be impounded` `District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) a State Court may order the document to be impounded` `Small Claims Tribunal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(1) a State Court may order the document to be impounded` `District Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(1) a State Court may order the document to be impounded` `General Division of the High Court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 63(2): the document has been impounded; there is an order signed by a judicial officer.
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the impounded document may be delivered out of the custody of the court or inspected` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the impounded document may be delivered out of the custody of the court or inspected` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(2) the impounded document may be delivered out of the custody of the court or inspected` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63(3) the court may direct the document to be sent to the Attorney-General, the Commissioner of Stamp Duties or any other officer of the Government` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(3) the court may direct the document to be sent to the Attorney-General, the Commissioner of Stamp Duties or any other officer of the Government` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 64 to 66`

#ASSERT `s 64(1)(a) the judicial officer is capable of accepting or taking another office of emolument or carrying on a business` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(1)(a) the judicial officer is capable of accepting or taking another office of emolument or carrying on a business` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 64(1)(b): the Chief Justice has approved; the advantage is salary or allowances.
#ASSERT `s 64(1)(b) the judicial officer may accept the fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(1)(b) the judicial officer may accept the fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64(1)(b) the judicial officer may accept the fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 64(2): approved; of the kind listed.
#ASSERT `s 64(2)(a) the judicial officer may be appointed to the body or hold the office` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64(2)(a) the judicial officer may be appointed to the body or hold the office` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(2)(a) the judicial officer may be appointed to the body or hold the office` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 64(2)(b) the judicial officer may receive the allowance or other honorarium` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 64(2)(b) the judicial officer may receive the allowance or other honorarium` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 64(2)(b) the judicial officer may receive the allowance or other honorarium` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 65: interested; approved; consent.
#ASSERT `s 65 the judicial officer may investigate, try or commit for trial the proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65 the judicial officer may investigate, try or commit for trial the proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65 the judicial officer may investigate, try or commit for trial the proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 65 the judicial officer may investigate, try or commit for trial the proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 65 the judicial officer may investigate, try or commit for trial the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 66 the officer may purchase or bid for the property` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66 the officer may purchase or bid for the property` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 67 and 68`

-- s 67(1): the holder; nominated; charged under (a); charged under (b).
#ASSERT `s 67(1) it is lawful for the District Judge to inquire into the matter in a summary manner` `District Judge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(1) it is lawful for the District Judge to inquire into the matter in a summary manner` `District Judge` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(1) it is lawful for the District Judge to inquire into the matter in a summary manner` `District Judge` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 67(1) it is lawful for the District Judge to inquire into the matter in a summary manner` `District Judge` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(1) it is lawful for the District Judge to inquire into the matter in a summary manner` Magistrate TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(2) the District Judge may summon and enforce the attendance of all necessary parties` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(2) the District Judge may summon and enforce the attendance of all necessary parties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may order repayment of the money extorted or payment of the money levied, damages and costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may order repayment of the money extorted or payment of the money levied, damages and costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may order repayment of the money extorted or payment of the money levied, damages and costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The fine: $100 for each offence is the ceiling.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may impose the fine upon the officer` TRUE TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may impose the fine upon the officer` TRUE TRUE 101 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may impose the fine upon the officer` TRUE FALSE 50 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(3) the District Judge may impose the fine upon the officer` FALSE TRUE 50 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(4) the officer is incapable of being an officer of the State Courts` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(4) the officer is incapable of being an officer of the State Courts` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 67(5) an appeal lies to the Chief Justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(5) an appeal lies to the Chief Justice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 67(6) the decision of the Chief Justice is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 67(6) the decision of the Chief Justice is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 68(1): in the discharge of judicial duty; in good faith believed to have jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `s 68(1) the judicial officer is liable to be sued for the act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(1) the judicial officer is liable to be sued for the act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(1) the judicial officer is liable to be sued for the act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 68(2): charged with executing process; the suit is within (a) or (b); knowingly in excess.
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the officer is liable to be sued` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the officer is liable to be sued` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the officer is liable to be sued` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the officer is liable to be sued` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the bar on suing the officer applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the bar on suing the officer applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the bar on suing the officer applies` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(2) the bar on suing the officer applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(3) the officer is deemed to have acted knowingly in excess of his or her authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(3) the officer is deemed to have acted knowingly in excess of his or her authority` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 68(4): the kind of person; for the purposes of mediation; good faith; no fraud or wilful misconduct.
#ASSERT `s 68(4) the person is liable to be sued for the act` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 68(4) the person is liable to be sued for the act` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(4) the person is liable to be sued for the act` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(4) the person is liable to be sued for the act` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68(4) the person is liable to be sued for the act` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 70`

-- s 70(1): a written law allows the action; the petition provisions have been amended; the action is pending; the Court thinks just and expedient.
#ASSERT `s 70(1) the Court may order the pending action or application to be converted and continued by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 70(1) the Court may order the pending action or application to be converted and continued by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 70(1) the Court may order the pending action or application to be converted and continued by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70(1) the Court may order the pending action or application to be converted and continued by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70(1) the Court may order the pending action or application to be converted and continued by way of a writ of summons or an originating summons` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may by order direct that a class or description of pending actions or applications be converted` `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 70(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may by order direct that a class or description of pending actions or applications be converted` `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may by order direct that a class or description of pending actions or applications be converted` `Presiding Judge of the State Courts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70(2) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts may by order direct that a class or description of pending actions or applications be converted` `District Judge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 70(3)(a) the converted action or application is continued in accordance with the relevant written law and the practice and procedure in force at the time of the conversion` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 70(3)(a) the converted action or application is continued in accordance with the relevant written law and the practice and procedure in force at the time of the conversion` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 70(3)(b) the Court may give the parties directions as to the conduct and costs of the action or application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 70(3)(b) the Court may give the parties directions as to the conduct and costs of the action or application` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 70(3)(b) the Court may give the parties directions as to the conduct and costs of the action or application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The regulative rules, run with #TRACE (a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on this binary; the same prohibitions are asserted above as decision functions).
#TRACE `s 64(1)(b) duty: a judicial officer must not accept fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A judicial officer` DOES `accept fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages other than salary and allowances` AT 4
#TRACE `s 65 duty: a judicial officer must not investigate, try or commit for trial a proceeding in which the officer is a party or personally interested` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `A judicial officer` DOES `investigate, try or commit for trial a proceeding in which the judicial officer is a party or personally interested` AT 1
#TRACE `s 66 duty: an officer of the State Courts having a duty in connection with a sale must not purchase or bid for the property` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `An officer of a State Court` DOES `purchase or bid for property sold in connection with a duty of the officer` AT 1
